{
    "description": "The two identifier rules every family repo applies: what a did:oc is, and the form an email address is stored and looked up in. Read by auth-core (src/__tests__/identifiers.test.ts) and sdk-py (tests/test_identifiers.py), so a Node site and a Python site agree. A did:oc is did:oc: and 32 lowercase hex digits, with nothing before or after it. An email is trimmed of exactly the characters JavaScript's String.prototype.trim removes, then lower-cased.",
